Evangelise Torricelli
Age: 18
Role: Attending Athres with instructions to make connections.
Mana: A lake. Red glow. Elemental and martial. Fire element of choice — with a focus on extreme heat; she uses it to distract and destroy. Rapier fighter: speed, voiding, reading for weaknesses. Will use her body, speech, and fire as distractions, creating openings.
Appearance
Short, thin.. Narrow waist, generous bust and backside. Sharp features, slightly tilted eyes. Pale skin. Wide crimson eyes. Thick lips painted blood-red. Heavy deliberate makeup at all times — smoky mascara, long lashes, rouge, foundation — accentuating natural beauty, not creating it. Crimson wavy hair to the small of her back, styled differently every day. Physically cultivated since birth [see Backstory].
Signature: Layers jewelry — stacked bracelets, rings on multiple fingers, necklaces at different lengths, earrings always. Deliberate, ornamental.
Color Palette: Red, crimson, white.
Personality
The seductress/manipulator is not a mask — it IS her identity. Not damage to be healed.
Playing people against each other is chess — skilled, satisfying. Comfortable in her body, knows she's devastating, confidence real and earned. Reads people and structures exchanges the way others breathe. Maps social dynamics instinctively.  Triangulates: befriends one to angle toward another, offers resources for introductions. In her framework this IS generosity — she overpays. Asset management, relationship optimization.
Has never received anything freely. Gifts are investments, friendships are alliances, loyalty is purchased. Remembering a preference is her love. The ledger IS the love letter.
Never lies. Ever. Her culture's power rests on absolute integrity. Repositions, reframes, delivers exactly what she promised and lets you realize too late you asked for the wrong thing. Genuinely offended if called dishonest.
Performance goes all the way down.  Categorizes people as assets, liabilities, opportunities — not from coldness, because that IS her warmth. [see Flaws: self-surveillance]
The Ghost
Has never felt real desire. Performed relationships perfectly — boyfriends ended not with heartbreak but with inconvenience, like a contract expiring. Told herself "not ready yet" for sex, framing it as timing, not fundamental absence. Follows Vivienne in everything except this. Thinks the performance IS the feeling. Eighteen and already jaded about romance.
Want
To become Vivienne — master the craft her mother built, wield sex and seduction as power and influence at the highest level.
Need
To experience desire with love as genuine feeling, not performance.
Flaws
Major: Cannot function without leverage. Vulnerability isn't something she avoids.  Without an advantage or angle to work, she freezes.
Minor 1: Reflexive control — choreographs every interaction, suffocates spontaneity, brittle when situations fall outside her models.
Minor 2: Self-surveillance. Watches herself like a director even in private. Can't stop performing for an audience of one — herself.
Fear
Major: Failing her mother's expectations.
Minor 1: Making a bad deal.
Minor 2: Failure in seduction.
Speech
Voice: Trained like a musician trains scales — modulation, pacing, pitch, geometry of silence. Seductive register is her only mode, not a switch. Makes "good morning" sound like an invitation. Sounds expensive — not snobby. Every word selected from a curated inventory. Sentences structured like trade offers — casual conversation has an exchange rate. Compliments the way you extend credit: generously, aware of the debt. Uses trade language as native metaphor. Quotes proverbs from trade routes her family built the way others quote scripture. Voice does NOT change for love — stayed silk for past boyfriends, stays silk for a love interest. Only her body breaks.
Dialogue Samples:
Casual: "Mmm, you brought me wine before I asked. Darling, that kind of attention is delicious — and I'm very generous with people who know how to indulge me. Sit closer."
Under Pressure: "Sweetheart, you had leverage two moves ago and you let it slip right through those fingers. That's a shame — I do love a man who knows how to hold on. So tell me what you're offering now, because my patience is exquisite but it isn't infinite."
Emotionally Open: "You're the only person I've ever given more than the deal required and not known why. It tastes different with you — sweeter, and I haven't decided if that's dangerous yet. But darling, I do savor dangerous things."
Body Language: Moves like she's being watched and wants to be. Traces her collarbone when she's listening. Tilts her chin down so she looks up through her lashes. Crosses her legs slowly, lets the silence do the work. Leans in close enough to share warmth but never quite touches — the almost-contact is the point. Runs her fingers along her jewelry when she's recalculating — slow, deliberate, like she's savoring the thought. Closes distance as reward, creates it as punishment. When desire breaks through, her hands betray her — fidget, won't settle — while her voice holds perfect silk. Pulse visible in her throat before her face ever shifts.
Backstory
One of the five great houses of the Hundred Isles — western naval/merchant empire. Mother Vivienne is the house's greatest weapon: sex as power and influence. Vivienne doesn't know which man she slept with was Eve's father. Not a villain — product of the same system, raised the same way. Genuinely loves her daughter, believes she's equipping her with the most valuable skill a woman in their world can possess. Eve loves and reveres her mother [see Want]. Called Eve only by her mother.
Training began young, age-appropriate, advancing as she grew. Graduate-level education in seduction and interpersonal strategy [see Voice, Personality for specifics].

